'' RUN: 'v = v & "def"' over a type that EXTENDS ZSTRING, through 'operator let( byref as zstring )':
'' a concatenation has no address, and the let's argument declined (TKO0994; manual
'' udt/extendszstring1 and 2; fbc-examples repro ice11). Now the descriptor's characters -- and
'' 'v &= x' with no 'operator &=' is 'v = v & x', as fbc lowers it.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/extends-zstring-concat.bas -o tests/codegen/extendszstringconcat.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0994
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/extendszstringconcat.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/extendszstringconcat.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: xabcdefy!xabcdefy!
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: [ab  c]
